<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Framework resource overlay for gaokun3.
  Fed to Soong by DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS in device.mk; the path mirrors the
  framework-res module's own resource directory.
-->
<resources>

    <!--
      Render at 120 Hz instead of 60.

      The panel has two modes and the *hardware* one already in use is 120 Hz
      (SurfaceFlinger: activeMode vsyncRate=120.00 Hz, vsync period 8.33 ms).
      What pinned the render rate to 60 was this framework default:
      frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/config.xml:5870 ships
      config_defaultRefreshRate = 60, and the scheduler duly configured itself
      for 60 Hz work (app duration 16666682 ns, SF duration 15666682 ns).

      ⚠️ Settings.System.peak_refresh_rate does NOT fix this — measured: setting
      it to 120 left the scheduler durations at 16.67 ms. The base/default rate
      is what governs, not the peak.

      Pinning rather than using config_defaultPeakRefreshRate=120 with
      config_defaultRefreshRate=0: the 60 Hz and 120 Hz modes sit in *different*
      mode groups (group=2 and group=1), so moving between them is a full
      non-seamless modeset rather than a seamless switch. Pinning the mode the
      panel is already in avoids that entirely.

      Cost is power: 120 Hz composites twice as often. Acceptable here because
      the GPU is nowhere near loaded — under Genshin at maximum settings it
      spends 91% of its time at its *lowest* 270 MHz step and peaks at 690 MHz.
      To go back to 60, set this to 60 and rebuild.
    -->
    <integer name="config_defaultRefreshRate">120</integer>

    <!--
      Take headset jack insertion from an input device rather than from
      /sys/class/switch/h2w.

      WiredAccessoryManager has two ways to learn that something was plugged
      into the jack. The default is the legacy switch class: it opens
      /sys/class/switch/h2w and listens for uevents. That directory does not
      exist on this machine and never will, because mainline has no h2w
      driver; measured on device: "ls /sys/class/switch/" is ENOENT. So the
      framework never learned about the jack at all, which is why plugging
      headphones in did nothing even once the audio path itself worked.

      With this true, WiredAccessoryManager consumes SW_HEADPHONE_INSERT and
      SW_MICROPHONE_INSERT from an ordinary evdev switch device instead. That
      source already exists and is already being read: the ALSA jack shows up
      as input device "SC8280XP-HUAWEI-GAOKUN3 Headset Jack" (event12) with
      SW bitmask 0xd4, which is HEADPHONE_INSERT, MICROPHONE_INSERT,
      LINEOUT_INSERT and VIDEOOUT_INSERT, and dumpsys input already classifies
      it as "KEYBOARD | SWITCH" with a live Switch Input Mapper. Nothing was
      missing on the kernel side; only this flag.

      Pairs with the Wired Headphone / Wired Headset device ports added to
      audio/primary_audio_policy_configuration.xml, which is what turns the
      resulting connection event into an actual ALSA device.
    -->
    <bool name="config_useDevInputEventForAudioJack">true</bool>

    <!--
      Android 16 desktop windowing: deliberately turned OFF.

      It was switched on briefly and switched back off at the user's request:
      on this tablet it puts every app into a freeform window, which is
      disruptive for normal use.

      ⚠️★ These must be explicit `false` overrides, not just "leave them out".
      crDroid turns desktop mode on for **every** device:

        vendor/lineage/overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values/
        config.xml:98   <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">true</bool>

      ⚠️★ And writing `false` **here** does not work either. Measured twice:
      the build assertion still reported `config_isDesktopModeSupported 还是
      true` with this file saying false. In this tree
      **PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS (vendor/lineage) outranks
      DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS (this file)** — the opposite of the usual
      claim that the device overlay wins. Our other values here work only
      because vendor/lineage does not touch them (checked name by name:
      config_isDesktopModeSupported is the single conflict).
      The actual disable is done by scripts/crdroid-tree-fixes.py, which
      edits vendor/lineage/overlay/common directly. The entries below are
      kept only to state intent.

      Removing our own entry therefore changed nothing — the build assertion
      caught it (`config_isDesktopModeSupported 还是 true`). Ours is a
      DEVICE_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS overlay, which outranks vendor/lineage's
      PRODUCT_PACKAGE_OVERLAYS, so an explicit false here wins.

      ★ This also corrects an earlier misreading: the upstream reference
      (dragon-lineage's Radxa Dragon commit d480d02) sets *only*
      config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops, and that is in fact correct and
      sufficient for a Lineage-based tree, because Lineage already supplies
      config_isDesktopModeSupported=true. Checking AOSP's default (false)
      without checking the ROM's own overlays is what led to the wrong call.

      ⚠️ There is no runtime way back — the developer-options toggle can only
      force desktop mode ON. Measured on device:

        show_desktop_experience_dev_option = true

      and DesktopModeFlags.getToggleOverrideFromSystem() short-circuits on it:

        if (Flags.showDesktopExperienceDevOption()) {
            if (DesktopExperienceFlags.getToggleOverride()) return OVERRIDE_ON;
            return ToggleOverride.OVERRIDE_UNSET;      // never OVERRIDE_OFF
        }

      so Settings.Global "override_desktop_mode_features" is dead here —
      verified: writing 0 changed nothing. "Off by default, opt in later" is
      likewise not expressible, because canEnterDesktopMode() is
      isDeviceEligibleForDesktopMode() && ENABLE_DESKTOP_WINDOWING_MODE, the
      aconfig flag is already true, and being eligible at all therefore means
      "always on".

      ⇒ To enable desktop windowing again, flip these two to true and rebuild.
    -->
    <bool name="config_isDesktopModeSupported">false</bool>
    <bool name="config_canInternalDisplayHostDesktops">false</bool>
    <bool name="config_isDesktopModeDevOptionSupported">false</bool>


    <!--
      TODO A0 的根因：这台机器从来没有过导航栏，于是手势导航的返回手势
      在物理上就不存在。

      实测（2026-08-24，桌面模式已关、navigation_mode=2 的干净状态）：
        dumpsys window windows  → 窗口列表里【只有 StatusBar，没有 NavigationBar】
        SysUiState              → hasNavigationBar=false
        InsetsSource mandatorySystemGestures
                                → frame=[0,0][1600,42] sideHint=TOP
                                   —— 只有顶部一条，左右两侧没有任何手势区
        mSystemGestureExclusion → SkRegion()（空，不是被应用屏蔽掉的）

      手势导航的返回处理器（SystemUI 的 EdgeBackGestureHandler）是随
      NavigationBar 组件创建的。没有导航栏 ⇒ 没有处理器 ⇒ 也没有左右手势
      inset，边缘往里滑什么都不会发生。

      AOSP 的默认值是 false（core/res/res/values/config.xml:2771，注释说
      "in the future this may be autodetected"）—— 那是给有实体按键的机器
      准备的。本机没有实体导航键，必须自己声明。我们此前【从未声明过】。

      ⚠️ 之前 A0 一直挂着"假说未证实"，怀疑是桌面模式的 freeform 窗口。
      那个假说是错的：桌面模式已经关了、窗口是 fullscreen，手势照样没有。

      ★ Lineage 不覆盖这一项（逐名核对过 vendor/lineage 的 common overlay），
      所以设备 overlay 在这里是有效的 —— 不像 config_isDesktopModeSupported
      那样要绕到 crdroid-tree-fixes.py 去改。
    -->
    <bool name="config_showNavigationBar">true</bool>

    <!--
      ★ NTP 服务器（TODO B22，#122）。AOSP 默认只有 ntp://time.android.com
      （core/res/res/values/config.xml:2787），它在国内不可达 —— 2026-09-24 设备上实测：
        cmd network_time_update_service force_refresh      → false
        settings put global ntp_server ntp.aliyun.com 后再刷 → true，时钟当场纠正 41 分钟
      而 mLastAutoSystemClockTimeSet=null（这次开机从没同步成功过）。

      LineageOS 其实给中国配了服务器，但放在 values-mcc460 里
      （vendor/lineage/overlay/common/frameworks/base/core/res/res/values-mcc460/config.xml:25）
      —— 要插着国内 SIM 才生效，本机没有基带，永远落不到那份。

      框架按列表顺序挨个试、失败就试下一个，成功的那个下次排最前
      （core/java/android/util/NtpTrustedTime.java:350-366），所以全球的放第一个、
      国内三个（与 Lineage 那份相同）跟在后面：国外用户不受影响，国内用户第一次多等一个超时（5 s）。
      ⚠️ 设置项 ntp_server 优先于这里（NtpTrustedTime.java:647-653）；开发机上手动设过的话，
         验证这份覆盖前先 settings delete global ntp_server。
    -->
    <string-array translatable="false" name="config_ntpServers">
        <item>ntp://time.android.com</item>
        <item>ntp://ntp.aliyun.com</item>
        <item>ntp://ntp.tencent.com</item>
        <item>ntp://ntp.ntsc.ac.cn</item>
    </string-array>

</resources>
